From 74b46690cafbb3ea0e918f99bfee09789ceaefd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:18:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] pinctrl: hisilicon: add the hi3798mv2x IOCONFIG pinctrl
 driver

Add the Hi3798MV200 IOCONFIG pin tables on top of the framework: the 66
pins with their per-pin mux lists and the function groups.

A5 and D5 stay out of the RGMII group: their per-pin tables, which are
what the framework applies at runtime, offer GPIO and CLKOUT, and PMC
and GPIO, so a request for RGMII on either pin would pass group
validation and only fail with -ENOENT while the state is applied.
Cross-checking the function lists against the per-pin tables turns up no
other disagreement.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/hisilicon/Kconfig             |  11 +
 drivers/pinctrl/hisilicon/Makefile            |   1 +
 .../pinctrl/hisilicon/pinctrl-hi3798mv2x.c    | 673 ++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 685 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/pinctrl/hisilicon/pinctrl-hi3798mv2x.c

--- a/drivers/pinctrl/hisilicon/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/hisilicon/Kconfig
@@ -14,4 +14,15 @@ config PINCTRL_HISTB
 	help
 	  Support HiSTB SoCs pinctrl module
 
+menu "HiSTB pinctrl drivers"
+	depends on PINCTRL_HISTB
+
+config PINCTRL_HI3798MV2X
+	tristate "HiSilicon Hi3798MV2X pinctrl driver"
+	depends on PINCTRL_HISTB
+	help
+	  Support IOCONFIG core on Hi3798MV2X SoCs
+
+endmenu
+
 endif
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/hisilicon/Makefile
